# Map notes for the other Dutch towns, English source. slug: (neighbourhoods, water, streets).
T = {
'hoofddorp': (
 'The centre lies where the Hoofdweg and the Kruisweg cross. Floriande, Toolenburg and Overbos are large newer districts, and Pax and Bornholm sit closer to the old village.',
 'The Ringvaart circles the whole Haarlemmermeer polder, and Floriande is built on a cluster of islands. Ponds and lakes fill the Haarlemmermeerse Bos on the edge of town.',
 'The polder grid sets the rules: long straight roads and ditches at right angles, with the newer districts curving gently inside the rectangles.'),
'zaandam': (
 'The old centre lies by the Dam and the station. The Rosmolenwijk and Kogerveld are older districts, while Poelenburg, Pelders en Hoornseveld and Westerwatering spread out to the west.',
 'The Zaan flows into the Voorzaan and the North Sea Canal at the south of town. Ditches and small lakes of the peat meadows edge the map in the north.',
 'The oldest streets follow the dikes on both sides of the Zaan in long ribbons. Behind them the twentieth century districts form neat, regular blocks.'),
'alkmaar': (
 'The old town sits inside the singel. Oudorp, Daalmeer and Huiswaard lie to the north and east, and Overdie and De Mare fill the rest of the map.',
 'The star shaped singelgracht wraps around the centre, the Noordhollandsch Kanaal runs along its west side, and canals such as the Luttik Oudorp run through the old town.',
 'Inside the star, streets like the Langestraat and the Laat run in long parallel lines. Outside it the districts fan out along the roads to the villages around town.'),
'purmerend': (
 'The old town lies around the Koemarkt. Overwhere and Wheermolen are older districts, and Weidevenne is a large new district built on islands in the south.',
 'The Where flows through the centre, the Noordhollandsch Kanaal passes along the town, and Weidevenne is laced with canals. The ring canals of the Beemster and the Purmer edge the map.',
 'The compact old centre gives way to the dead straight roads of the polders. To the north the Beemster grid, a World Heritage site, draws its perfect squares.'),
'amstelveen': (
 'The Stadshart is the modern centre. Elsrijk and Randwijk are green and quiet, Westwijk and Middenhoven are newer, and the Oude Dorp keeps its village character.',
 'The Amstel follows the eastern edge, the Poel lake lies near Bovenkerk, and the long straight Bosbaan cuts through the Amsterdamse Bos in the west.',
 'Long lanes like the Amsterdamseweg and the Bovenkerkerweg run north to south. Between them the post war districts curve around parks and canals.'),
'hilversum': (
 'The centre lies around the Groest and the Kerkbrink. Trompenberg and Boomberg are villa districts, Kerkelanden is a green post war district, and the Media Park lies to the north.',
 'There is little water in this sandy town. The Hilversums Kanaal starts on the west side, and the lakes of Loosdrecht lie just beyond the edge of the map.',
 'Curving villa lanes wind between the woods and the heath. Around the centre the streets form an irregular web, typical of a town that grew from a heath village.'),
'heerhugowaard': (
 'The centre lies around the Middenwaard. Butterhuizen, Huygenhoek and the Edelstenenwijk are residential districts, and the Stad van de Zon is built around a lake in the south.',
 'A ring canal follows the edge of the old lake bed, the polder ditches run in straight lines, and the lake of the Stad van de Zon sits in the middle of its district.',
 'The Middenweg runs dead straight through the polder from south to north. The districts fill the rectangles between the old polder roads.'),
'hoorn': (
 'The old town lies between the harbour and the Grote Noord. Kersenboogerd, Risdam and Grote Waal are newer districts, and Zwaag is a village that grew into the town.',
 'The Markermeer forms the whole southern edge. The Binnenhaven and Buitenhaven cut into the old town, and canals and the old moat circle the centre.',
 'The old streets run in long lines from the harbour inland, with the Grote Noord as the main street. Outside the old moat the districts follow a modern plan.'),
'ijmuiden': (
 'Oud IJmuiden lies near the locks, Zeewijk is a large post war district by the dunes, and Driehuis and Velsen-Zuid lie to the east. Velsen-Noord lies across the canal.',
 'The North Sea Canal and its locks, including one of the largest sea locks in the world, form the northern edge. The fishing harbour and the Forteiland lie at the mouth.',
 'The Kennemerlaan is the long main street. Zeewijk follows a planned post war layout, and the dunes behind the beach stay almost empty on the map.'),
'bussum': (
 'The centre lies around the station and the Brinklaan. Het Spiegel is a villa district, Bussum Zuid is green and quiet, and the old fortress of Naarden lies to the north.',
 'There is little water in this sandy town. The moats of Naarden and the Gooimeer lie to the north, and ponds dot the woods and estates around town.',
 'Curving lanes with villas wind through the woods. The railway cuts the town in two, and long roads lead out towards Naarden, Huizen and Hilversum.'),
'den-helder': (
 'The old centre lies near Willemsoord, the former naval shipyard. Nieuw Den Helder and De Schooten are residential districts, and Julianadorp lies to the south.',
 'The Marsdiep separates the town from Texel, the naval harbour lies by the water, and the Noordhollandsch Kanaal ends here after its long route from Amsterdam.',
 'Dikes and forts of the old Stelling Den Helder ring the town. Inside them the streets form a regular grid, with dunes and beach along the west.'),
'naaldwijk': (
 'The old village lies around the church square. Newer districts such as Hoogeland spread out around it, and greenhouse land fills every other part of the map.',
 'The Naaldwijkse Vaart runs through town, and countless ditches and water basins for the greenhouses make a fine blue pattern across the Westland.',
 'Greenhouses line up in long straight blocks along the polder roads. The old centre is the only part where the streets curve.'),
'alphen-aan-den-rijn': (
 'The centre lies along the Oude Rijn. Kerk en Zanen and Ridderveld are large residential districts, and Oudshoorn lies on the other side of the river.',
 'The Oude Rijn crosses the town from east to west, the Gouwe branches off to the south, and the Aarkanaal leads north. Polder ditches surround the town.',
 'The streets run parallel to the river, with the Hooftstraat as the main street. The newer districts are laid out around canals and parks.'),
'spijkenisse': (
 'The old village lies around the church by the Oude Maas. Groenewoud, Waterland, Maaswijk and De Akkers were built from the 1970s onward, when the town grew fast.',
 'The Oude Maas forms the northern edge, crossed by the Spijkenisserbrug. Canals and ponds run through every district, fitting their names.',
 'The new districts were planned with curving roads and green belts. The metro line from Rotterdam runs through the middle of town.'),
'schiedam': (
 'The old centre sits between the harbours. Oost, Nieuwland and Groenoord are older residential districts, and Kethel and Woudhoek lie to the north and west.',
 'The Schie flows into the Nieuwe Maas, the Lange Haven and the Korte Haven run through the old town, and the singel with its windmills marks the old walls.',
 'The old streets follow the harbours in long narrow lines. Beyond the singel the districts form regular blocks, with the A20 motorway along the north.'),
'voorburg': (
 'Oud Voorburg lies along the Herenstraat. Bovenveen, Essesteijn and Damsigt are leafy districts, and Voorburg West borders The Hague.',
 'The Vliet runs along the town from Leiden to Delft. Hofwijck and other estates lie by the water, and ponds dot the parks.',
 'The Herenstraat follows the old village line, and wide lanes such as the Laan van Nieuw Oosteinde run towards The Hague. Many streets are lined with trees.'),
'gouda': (
 'The old town lies around the Markt. Kort Haarlem and Korte Akkeren are older districts, Bloemendaal and Goverwelle lie to the north and east.',
 'The Gouwe and the Hollandse IJssel meet at the south of town. The Turfsingel and Kattensingel follow the old walls, and canals run straight through the centre.',
 'The triangular Markt sits at the heart of a compact web of streets such as the Lange Groenendaal. Around the singels the districts follow the polder lines.'),
'vlaardingen': (
 'The old centre lies between the Markt and the Oude Haven. Westwijk, Holy and Ambacht are residential districts, and Oost lies towards Schiedam.',
 'The Nieuwe Maas forms the southern edge, the Oude Haven cuts deep into the town, and the Vlaardingervaart leads north. The Broekpolder adds lakes and green.',
 'The Hoogstraat is the old main street along the harbour. The post war districts are laid out in long rows with green between them.'),
'hellevoetsluis': (
 'The old fortress town sits by the harbour. Nieuwenhoorn is an old village that grew into the town, and De Struytse Hoeck and Ravense Hoek are newer districts.',
 'The Haringvliet forms the southern edge. The Kanaal door Voorne starts at the old harbour, and moats surround the bastions of the fortress.',
 'Inside the fortress the streets form a small regular grid. Outside it the districts follow curving roads, laid out around water and green.'),
'capelle-aan-den-ijssel': (
 'Schollevaar, Oostgaarde and Middelwatering are large residential districts. Capelle-West borders Rotterdam, and the old village lies along the dike.',
 'The Hollandse IJssel forms the southern edge, crossed by the Algerabrug. The Schollebos and many lakes and canals add blue to the districts.',
 'The old village follows the river dike. The newer districts were planned with long curving roads, green strips and water between the blocks.'),
'katwijk': (
 'Katwijk aan Zee lies by the beach, Katwijk aan den Rijn lies inland, and Rijnsburg and Valkenburg are villages within the municipality. Hoornes is a newer district.',
 'The Oude Rijn reaches the sea here through the old outlet sluices of 1807. The North Sea and the dunes form the western edge.',
 'The boulevard follows the coast, and the Voorstraat is the old main street. The streets of the old fishing village are short and close together.'),
'rijswijk': (
 'Oud Rijswijk lies around the Herenstraat. Te Werve, Leeuwendaal and the Bomen en Bloemenbuurt are residential districts, and Rijswijk Buiten is the newest.',
 'The Vliet runs along the eastern side. Ponds and canals fill the Wilhelminapark and the green estates such as Te Werve.',
 'The Herenstraat follows the old village line. The districts around it form a calm grid, merging into The Hague and Delft without clear edges.'),
'pijnacker': (
 'Pijnacker has its old centre along the main road. Koningshof, Klapwijk, Ackerswoude and Tolhek are residential districts, and Nootdorp is the second village of the municipality.',
 'The Dobbeplas lies near Nootdorp, the Ackerdijkse Plassen lie to the south, and polder ditches draw lines across the land between the villages.',
 'The old village follows the road in a long line. The new districts are built in rectangles between the polder ditches.'),
'berkel-en-rodenrijs': (
 'The village centre lies along the main street. Rodenrijs lies to the south and the Westpolder is a large new district on the west side.',
 'Polder ditches and canals run in straight lines through the land. The Rottemeren lie a little to the east, and the Westpolder is built around water.',
 'The roads follow the old reclamation pattern in long straight lines. The RandstadRail station gives the newer districts their focus.'),
'oud-beijerland': (
 'The old centre lies along the harbour and the dike. Poortwijk and the Zinkweg area are residential districts, and new districts grow towards the fields.',
 'The Spui flows along the south west of town, and the old harbour leads to it. Creeks wind through the polders of the Hoeksche Waard.',
 'The oldest streets follow the dike in a long line. Around them the polders keep their straight roads and ditches.'),
'veenendaal': (
 'The centre lies around the Markt and the Oude Kerk. Dragonder, Petenbos, Engelenburg and Veenendaal Oost are residential districts.',
 'The town was built on peat, and old canals from that time still run through it. Ponds fill the parks, and the woods of the Heuvelrug lie to the west.',
 'The Hoofdstraat runs through the old centre, past the former textile mills. The newer districts follow a planned layout with green between the blocks.'),
'nieuwegein': (
 'Vreeswijk and Jutphaas are the old villages. Galecop, Batau, Fokkesteeg, Zuilenstein and Doorslag were built from the 1970s onward as a new town.',
 'The Merwedekanaal and the Lekkanaal cut through the town, the Lek forms the southern edge, and the old locks of Vreeswijk lie at the river.',
 'The new town was planned around the tram line to Utrecht. Its districts have curving roads, canals and green strips, with the city centre in the middle.'),
'zeist': (
 'The centre lies around the Slotlaan. Kerckebosch, Vollenhove and Crosestein are residential districts, and Den Dolder, Austerlitz and Huis ter Heide are villages nearby.',
 'Zeist lies on the dry sand of the Heuvelrug, so water is rare. Ponds and canals belong to Slot Zeist and the estates, and the Kromme Rijn flows to the south.',
 'Long straight lanes lead through the woods to the Slot. Around them villa streets curve, and the Zusterplein and Broederplein form a neat pair of squares.'),
'maarssen': (
 'The old village lies along the Vecht. Maarssenbroek is the large new district across the canal, built from the 1970s onward.',
 'The Vecht winds past the village, the Amsterdam Rijnkanaal cuts straight through, and the Maarsseveense Plassen lie to the north.',
 'The old village streets follow the river. Maarssenbroek was planned with curving roads around canals, and estates line the Vecht to the north.'),
'vianen': (
 'The old town lies inside the walls along the Voorstraat. Newer districts lie to the south, and Hagestein and Everdingen are villages nearby.',
 'The Lek forms the northern edge, the Merwedekanaal passes the town, and moats still circle the old walls.',
 'The old town is a small, regular grid with the wide Voorstraat in the middle, ending at the Lekpoort. Outside it the streets follow modern lines.'),
'woerden': (
 'The old town lies inside the singel. Molenvliet, Snel en Polanen and the Schilderskwartier are residential districts, and Harmelen is a village nearby.',
 'The Oude Rijn runs through the town, the singel with its bastions surrounds the centre, and polder ditches spread out in the Groene Hart.',
 'Inside the singel the streets are short and old, with the Rijnstraat as the main street. Outside it the districts follow the polder roads.'),
'houten': (
 'The old village lies in the middle, surrounded by Houten Noord and Houten Zuid. Castellum is a newer district in the south.',
 'Canals and ponds wind between the districts, and the Amsterdam Rijnkanaal runs along the west side of town.',
 'A ring road keeps cars on the outside, and each district can only be reached from that ring. Bike paths run straight to the station in the middle.'),
'driebergen': (
 'The centre lies along the Hoofdstraat. Rijsenburg is the second village that grew together with Driebergen, and country estates and villa areas fill the rest.',
 'There is little water on the Heuvelrug. Ponds belong to the estates, and the Kromme Rijn flows through the fields to the south.',
 'The Hoofdstraat follows the old road along the ridge, lined with estates. Lanes lead from it into the woods on the north side.'),
'ede': (
 'The centre lies around the station. Veldhuizen, Rietkampen and Kernhem are residential districts, and Bennekom is a village nearby.',
 'Ede lies on the dry sand of the Veluwe, so water is rare. The Valleikanaal runs through the fields to the west.',
 'The railway runs through the middle of town. The former barracks area is laid out as a new district, and the woods begin right where the streets end.'),
'doetinchem': (
 'The old centre lies around the Simonsplein. De Huet, Overstegen, Dichteren and Schöneveld are residential districts.',
 'The Oude IJssel curves through the town, and small streams flow into it from the fields of the Achterhoek.',
 'The centre has a compact web of old streets such as the Hamburgerstraat. Long roads lead out to the villages of the Achterhoek.'),
'barneveld': (
 'The old centre lies around the church. Veller and Vaarst are newer districts, and hamlets and farms lie all around.',
 'The Barneveldse Beek runs past the village, and the Valleikanaal lies further west. Ditches mark the fields of the Gelderse Vallei.',
 'The old streets meet at the church. Around them the newer districts form neat blocks, and country roads lead to the farms.'),
'harderwijk': (
 'The old town lies inside the walls. Stadsweiden and Drielanden are newer districts, and the Waterfront is a new district by the lake.',
 'The Veluwemeer forms the northern edge, with harbours and the boulevard along the shore.',
 'Inside the walls the old town has narrow streets such as the Donkerstraat. Outside them the districts spread towards the Veluwe.'),
'zutphen': (
 'The old town lies inside the walls. Leesten and the Waterkwartier are residential districts, and De Hoven lies across the IJssel.',
 'The IJssel forms the western edge, and the Berkel flows into it through the old town. Moats still follow parts of the walls.',
 'The old town has squares such as the Houtmarkt and the Zaadmarkt, and the Nieuwstad was a planned extension in the Middle Ages.'),
'helmond': (
 'The centre lies around the castle. Brandevoort and Dierdonk are newer districts, Rijpelberg and Mierlo-Hout lie to the west, and Stiphout to the north.',
 'The Zuid-Willemsvaart runs through the centre, the Eindhovens Kanaal ends here, and the castle stands in its moat.',
 'The canal cuts the town in two, with the centre on its east bank. Brandevoort is built like a walled village, with a canal around it.'),
'oss': (
 'The centre lies around the Heuvel. Ruwaard and Schadewijk are residential districts, and Berghem, Megen and Lith are villages within the municipality.',
 'The Maas flows to the north of town, and a canal leads from Oss to the river. Small streams run through the fields.',
 'Long roads lead out from the centre to the villages around it. Industrial areas lie along the canal on the north side.'),
'cuijk': (
 'The old centre lies along the Maas. Padbroek is a large residential district, and villages surround the town.',
 'The Maas forms the eastern edge, and the Kraaijenbergse Plassen make a big pattern of lakes to the north west.',
 'The old streets follow the river bank. Behind them the town spreads out in regular blocks towards the railway.'),
'veghel': (
 'The centre lies around the church. The Noordkade lies along the canal, and villages such as Erp and Mariaheide belong to the same municipality.',
 'The Zuid-Willemsvaart runs through the town, and the river Aa flows past it.',
 'The Hoofdstraat runs through the centre. Industrial areas line the canal, and country roads lead out to the villages.'),
'roosendaal': (
 'The centre lies around the Markt. Kalsdonk, Tolberg, Langdonk and Kortendijk are residential districts.',
 'The Roosendaalse Vliet flows to the north, and ponds lie in the parks. The woods of the border land are close by.',
 'The railway yard sits just north of the centre. Long roads lead out to Antwerp, Bergen op Zoom and Breda.'),
'bergen-op-zoom': (
 'The old centre lies around the Grote Markt. Gageldonk, Meilust and Fort-Zeekant are residential districts.',
 'The Oosterschelde lies to the west, the old harbour leads to it, and the Binnenschelde is a lake right next to town.',
 'The old town sits on the slope of the Brabantse Wal. Its streets meet at the Grote Markt, and the newer districts climb up the ridge.'),
'uden': (
 'The centre lies around the Markt. Bitswijk, Hoeven and Velmolen are residential districts, and Volkel lies to the east.',
 'Uden has no river, so the ponds in the parks and the fens of De Maashorst are the main water on the map.',
 'Long roads lead out from the Markt in all directions. The newer districts fill the space between them.'),
'oosterhout': (
 'The centre lies around De Heuvel. Oosterheide, Vrachelen and Dommelbergen are residential districts, and the old manor houses, the slotjes, lie around town.',
 'The Wilhelminakanaal runs along the north side, and ponds and moats belong to the slotjes.',
 'De Heuvel is a wide square where many streets meet. Around it the streets curve, with green lanes leading out to the woods.'),
'waalwijk': (
 'The centre lies along the Grotestraat. Sprang-Capelle and Waspik are villages within the municipality.',
 'The Bergsche Maas forms the northern edge, and a harbour leads from the town to the river.',
 'The town stretches along the main road, the old Langstraat. The sand dunes of the Loonse en Drunense Duinen lie to the south.'),
'venlo': (
 'The old town lies on the east bank of the Maas. Blerick lies across the river, Venlo-Oost and Tegelen spread out to the east and south.',
 'The Maas forms the main line on the map, with bridges between Venlo and Blerick. Ponds lie in the parks.',
 'The old town has a compact web of streets around the Markt. Long roads lead out to Germany, only a few kilometres away.'),
'sittard': (
 'The old town lies inside the former walls. Overhoven is a residential district, and Geleen forms one town with Sittard.',
 'The Geleenbeek and the Rode Beek flow through the area, and ponds lie in the parks.',
 'The old town is round, with streets meeting at the Markt. The German border runs just east of town.'),
'heerlen': (
 'The centre lies around the Pancratiusplein. Heerlerheide, Hoensbroek, Schandelen and Welten are districts, and old mining villages lie all around.',
 'Heerlen lies in the hills, and streams such as the Geleenbeek start here. Ponds lie in the parks and old mine areas.',
 'The streets climb and curve with the hills. The old mining districts form their own small grids around former shafts.'),
'roermond': (
 'The old town lies inside the former walls. Maasniel, Kapel in ’t Zand, Donderberg and Swalmen are districts.',
 'The Roer flows into the Maas here, and the Maasplassen spread out in a big pattern of lakes to the west.',
 'The old town is a compact web around the Munsterplein and the Markt. Long roads lead out to the villages along the Maas.'),
'weert': (
 'The centre lies around the Markt and the Sint-Martinuskerk. Leuken, Fatima, Moesel and Boshoven are residential districts.',
 'The Zuid-Willemsvaart curves past the town, and other canals meet near Nederweert. Fens lie in the woods of the Kempen.',
 'The old town has a compact web of streets. The districts grow outward along the roads to Belgium and Brabant.'),
'deventer': (
 'The old town lies around the Brink. Colmschate, Keizerslanden, Zandweerd and the Rivierenwijk are residential districts.',
 'The IJssel draws a wide curve along the old town. The Schipbeek flows into it from the east.',
 'The old town has a dense web of streets around the Brink and the Bergkwartier. The districts spread to the east, away from the river.'),
'almelo': (
 'The centre lies around the Grotestraat. De Riet and Ossenkoppelerhoek are large residential districts.',
 'Canals meet in Almelo: a side branch of the Twentekanaal and the canal to De Haandrik.',
 'Long roads lead out from the old centre. The former textile mills shaped the districts around them.'),
'hengelo': (
 'The centre lies around the Markt and the town hall. Hasseler Es, Berflo Es and Groot Driene are residential districts.',
 'The Twentekanaal runs along the south of town with a harbour, and streams such as the Drienerbeek flow through the parks.',
 'The railway and the canal shaped the plan. The districts spread out between them, with green estates around the edges.'),
'hardenberg': (
 'The centre lies by the Vecht. Heemse lies south of the river, and Baalderveld and Marslanden are newer districts.',
 'The Overijsselse Vecht winds through the town, and the canal to Almelo starts close by.',
 'The old streets follow the river. The newer districts spread out north and south, with fields all around.'),
'kampen': (
 'The old town lies along the IJssel. Brunnepe, the Hanzewijk and Onderdijks are residential districts, and IJsselmuiden lies across the river.',
 'The IJssel forms the eastern edge of the old town, close to where it reaches the Ketelmeer. Old moats lie behind the town.',
 'Long streets such as the Oudestraat run parallel to the river, crossed by short lanes. Two city gates still stand on the land side, and the Koornmarktspoort faces the river.'),
'borne': (
 'The old centre lies around the church. Bornsche Maten is a large new district on the west side of town.',
 'Small streams cross the fields, and Bornsche Maten is built around ponds and green.',
 'The old village streets meet near the church. Bornsche Maten has curving streets in a planned layout.'),
'oldenzaal': (
 'The old town lies around the basilica. The districts grow outward on all sides, with Zuid-Berghuizen in the south.',
 'Oldenzaal lies on high ground, so there is little water. Ponds lie in the parks and small streams flow through the fields.',
 'The old streets form an almost perfect circle around the basilica. Roads lead out from it to Germany and the villages around.'),
'haaksbergen': (
 'The centre lies around the church. Buurse and Sint Isidorushoeve are villages within the municipality.',
 'The Buurserbeek flows south of the village, and the moors of the Haaksbergerveen have pools and ditches.',
 'The village streets meet at the centre. Around it fields and estates make a fine pattern of lanes and woodland edges.'),
'losser': (
 'The village centre lies near the Dinkel. De Lutte, Overdinkel and Glane are villages within the municipality.',
 'The Dinkel meanders along the east side of the village, close to the German border.',
 'The village streets meet at the centre. Country roads wind between fields, heath and small woods.'),
'rijssen': (
 'The old centre lies near the Regge. Holten is a village within the same municipality.',
 'The Regge flows past the town, and small streams cross the fields to the east.',
 'The old streets meet near the church. The Holterberg and the Sallandse Heuvelrug rise to the west.'),
'nijverdal': (
 'The village centre lies around the Grotestraat. Residential districts spread out towards the hills.',
 'The Regge flows along the east side of the village.',
 'The streets follow the foot of the Sallandse Heuvelrug. The heath and woods begin right where the houses end.'),
'goor': (
 'The centre lies around the church. Delden is the other small town in the municipality of Hof van Twente.',
 'The Twentekanaal and its harbour run along the edge of town, and small streams cross the estates.',
 'The old streets meet at the centre. Around it the estates and fields make a fine pattern of lanes.'),
'vriezenveen': (
 'The village stretches along the main road. Westerhaar is a village to the north east.',
 'Canals from the peat era run beside the road, and ditches cross the fields.',
 'Vriezenveen is a ribbon village, built along one road for several kilometres. Side roads branch off at right angles into the fields.'),
'tubbergen': (
 'The village centre lies around the church. Albergen, Vasse and Geesteren are villages within the municipality.',
 'Small streams cross the fields, and the Dinkel valley lies to the east.',
 'Country roads wind between farms and small woods. The village streets meet at the church.'),
'ootmarsum': (
 'The old town sits on a hill around the church. Small residential districts lie around it.',
 'Streams run down from the hills to the Dinkel valley in the east.',
 'The old streets form a round plan around the church. Country roads lead out to the hills and the Kuiperberg.'),
'wierden': (
 'The village centre lies around the church. Enter is a village within the municipality.',
 'The Regge flows to the west, and small streams cross the fields.',
 'The railway runs through the middle of the village. The heath of the Wierdense Veld lies to the north.'),
'emmen': (
 'The centre lies around the Raadhuisplein and the Wildlands zoo. Angelslo, Emmerhout, Bargeres and Rietlanden are residential districts.',
 'Long straight canals from the peat era run to the east, and ponds lie in the woods around the dolmens.',
 'The old village streets curve around the centre. The newer districts follow planned layouts, with green strips between them.'),
'assen': (
 'The centre lies around the Brink. Kloosterveen, Marsdijk, Pittelo and Lariks are residential districts.',
 'The Drentsche Hoofdvaart starts in Assen, and ponds lie in the Asserbos.',
 'The old centre has a compact web around the Brink. The districts spread out between woods and fields.'),
'hoogeveen': (
 'The centre lies along the Hoofdstraat. Krakeel, Erflanden and Wolfsbos are residential districts, and Hollandscheveld is a village to the south.',
 'The Hoogeveensche Vaart runs past the town, a canal from the peat era.',
 'The Hoofdstraat runs in a dead straight line through town, following the old peat canal. Side streets branch off at right angles.'),
'sneek': (
 'The old town lies inside the canals. Tinga, Noorderhoek and Duinterpen are residential districts.',
 'Canals circle the old town, the Waterpoort stands over the water, and the Sneekermeer lies to the east.',
 'The old streets follow the canals in a compact web. Outside them the districts spread towards the lakes.'),
'drachten': (
 'The centre lies around the Raadhuisplein. De Wiken and De Drait are residential districts.',
 'The Drachtstervaart leads into the centre, and canals run through the districts. Lakes lie to the north.',
 'The streets follow the old peat canals in long lines. The Laweiplein became famous as a square without traffic lights or signs.'),
'heerenveen': (
 'The centre lies around the old peat canal. Skoatterwâld is a newer district, and Oranjewoud lies to the south east.',
 'The Schoterlandse Compagnonsvaart runs through the town, a canal from the peat era. Ponds lie in the woods of Oranjewoud.',
 'The old streets follow the canal in long lines. Thialf and the woods give the edges of the map large open shapes.'),
'joure': (
 'The old centre lies along the Midstraat. Residential districts spread out around it.',
 'Canals lead from Joure to the lakes nearby, such as the Langweerder Wielen and the Sneekermeer.',
 'The Midstraat runs through the centre in a long line. The newer districts are laid out around green and water.'),
'hoogezand': (
 'Hoogezand and Sappemeer form one long town. Foxhol and Kalkwijk lie nearby.',
 'The Winschoterdiep runs through the whole town, and the Zuidlaardermeer lies to the south.',
 'The town stretches for kilometres along the canal. Side streets branch off at right angles, following the old peat land.'),
'lelystad': (
 'The centre lies around the station. Atolwijk, Bolder and the Zuiderzeewijk are residential districts, and Batavia Stad lies by the water.',
 'The Markermeer forms the western edge, and canals run through the districts. The Oostvaardersplassen lie to the north east.',
 'Lelystad was planned on empty land, with separate roads for cars, bicycles and buses. The Houtribdijk leads across the water to Enkhuizen.'),
'emmeloord': (
 'The centre lies around the Poldertoren. Residential districts spread out around it, and a ring of villages lies further out.',
 'The main canals of the Noordoostpolder meet near the town, and ditches cross the fields in straight lines.',
 'Roads and canals run out from the centre in straight lines towards the villages. The polder grid fills everything in between.'),
'terneuzen': (
 'The old centre lies by the harbour. Residential districts spread out to the south, and Sluiskil and Axel lie nearby.',
 'The Westerschelde forms the northern edge, and the canal to Ghent starts here with large locks.',
 'The old streets lie close to the water. Industrial areas line the canal, and polder roads lead out to the villages.'),
'middelburg': (
 'The old town lies inside the star of canals. Dauwendaele and Mortiere are residential districts.',
 'The singels form an almost perfect star around the old town, and the Kanaal door Walcheren passes along its east side.',
 'The old streets meet at the Markt and the abbey. Outside the star the districts follow the roads to Vlissingen and Veere.'),
}
